    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d472">

                <pb facs="0606" n="492" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg492"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/3467: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-06-04T15:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 4, 1924—3
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received June 4—8:35 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>156. Italian Minister reminds me that he had formerly joined in note to the
                    Chinese Government regarding its responsibility for the Chinese Eastern Railway
                    under the terms of the Washington Conference resolution<anchor n="16"
                        xml:id="d472-f1"/> but says that in view of the recognition of Soviet Russia
                    by China he does not know what stand he should now take and desires to be
                    informed of the policy and attitude of the American Government. I should greatly
                    appreciate a statement for my own guidance also.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d472-f1" n="16" xml:id="d472-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram no. 253, Oct. 27, 1922, to the Minister in China, <ref
                        target="frus1922v01#pg_925"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>,
                        1922, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, p. 925</ref>; also telegram
                    no. 229, Nov. 17, 1922, from the Chargé in Italy, <ref
                        target="frus1922v01#pg_929"><hi rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, p.
                    929</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
